content.text:
Now write game.js. I'll write the full content. Need to be meticulous.

Let's think through save `version` and `hydrate` again:
```
function newState(){
 return {version:2, scene:'shop', player:{x:760,y:810,dir:'up'}, playtime:0, items:{}, clues:{}, flags:{}, notes:{}, cards:{}, deductions:{}, usedTopics:{}, discoveries:{}, newItems:{}, memory:{}, decor:{lamp:'amber',rug:'rose',sill:'fern',wall:'empty'}, ending:null, visited:{shop:true}, savedAt:null};
}
function hydrate(raw){
 const base=newState();
 if(!raw||raw.version!==2) return base;
 const s=Object.assign({}, base, raw);
 s.player=Object.assign({},base.player,raw.player||{});
 s.decor=Object.assign({},base.decor,raw.decor||{});
 ['items',...].forEach(k=>{s[k]=Object.assign({},base[k],raw[k]||{});});
 s.ending=raw.ending||null;
 s.scene=D.scenes[raw.scene]?raw.scene:'shop';
 s.playtime=raw.playtime||0;
 return s;
}
```
- Note `raw.version` may be 2. Good.

Effects:
```
const effect={
 item(id){ if(!S) return; if(!S.items[id]){S.items[id]=true; S.newItems[id]=true; const o=D.objects[id]; toast('Into the satchel', o?o.name:id,'+'); queueSave(); renderInventoryIfOpen(); }},
 clue(id,silent){...},
 flag(k,v){ S.flags[k]=v===undefined?true:v; queueSave(); updateThought(); updateHUD(); },
 note(id){ S.notes[id]=true; queueSave(); },
 card(id){ if(!S.cards[id]){S.cards[id]=true; toast('Pinned to the board',D.cards[id]?D.cards[id].title:id,'⌖'); queueSave(); checkReady(); renderBoardIfOpen(); } }
};
```
- clue flush:
```
let clueTimer=null, clueBatch=[];
clue(id,silent){ if(S.clues[id]) return; S.clues[id]=true; if(!silent) clueBatch.push(id); queueSave(); updateThought(); updateHUD(); if(journal open) renderJournal(); if(board open) renderBoard(); if(silent) { checkReady(); } else { clearTimeout(clueTimer); clueTimer=setTimeout(flushClues,80);} }
```
- `flushClues`: if batch length 1 toast title; else toast "New details" `${n} new details...`; play discover? Play once. `AUDIO.play('discover')` maybe every clue; do once.
- checkReady after.
- `silent` still play discover? inspect plays separately.
- `card` batch maybe no.

- Note: effect.flag called with true. Good.

- `renderInventoryIfOpen` check overlayStack includes inventory.
- `renderBoardIfOpen`.
- `renderJournalIfOpen`.

- `checkReady`:
```
if(readyToDecide() && !S.flags.readyNotified){S.flags.readyNotified=true; toast('The whole story','The counter is waiting...','✓'); AUDIO.play('chime'); queueSave();}
```
- But if user returns after ending? readyToDecide still true if items letter etc. In kept ending, letterFound true, juneStory true, deductions. S.ending set; readyToDecide should return false if S.ending. Add `if(S.ending) return false;`.
- `readyToDecide` requires !S.ending.

- `updateHUD` status.

- `renderBoard` might call checkReady? no.

- Board deductions effect: set S.deductions[id]=true; queueSave; toast; if all core -> checkReady; renderBoard; updateHUD.

- Toast title text for clue maybe too long. Fine.

- `escape` no.

Now dialogue functions. Need maintain `dialogueState`:
```
{
 node, stack: [], lineIndex:0, typing:false, timer:null, fullText:'', shown:0, awaitingClose:false, parent:null, portrait:null
}
```
`renderNode(node, opts)`:
```
const st=dialogueState; if(!st) return;
st.node=node; st.awaitingClose=false; st.lineIndex=0;
$('dlgTopics').innerHTML='';
const dlg=$('dialogue');
if(node.speaker){
 const c=D.characters[node.speaker]||...
 dlg.classList.remove('narration');
 $('dlgPortraitWrap').style.display='';
 $('dlgName').textContent=c.name;
 $('dlgRole').textContent=c.role;
 if(st.portrait!==node.speaker){ A.drawPortrait($('dlgPortrait'), c.portrait||node.speaker); st.portrait=node.speaker; }
 $('dlgClose').hidden = node.allowLeave===false;
} else {
 dlg.classList.add('narration');
 $('dlgPortraitWrap').style.display='none';
 $('dlgName').textContent='';
 $('dlgRole').textContent='';
 $('dlgClose').hidden = node.allowLeave===false;
}
if(node.onEnter) node.onEnter();
if(node.note) effect.note(node.note);
if(opts&&opts.skipLines){
 st.lineIndex=Math.max(0,(node.lines||[]).length-1);
 $('dlgText').textContent=(node.lines||[])[st.lineIndex]||'';
 $('dlgText').classList.toggle('narration', !node.speaker);
 finishLines();
} else {
 showLine();
}
```
- For skipLines if node has no lines, finishLines.
- `showLine`:
```
const lines=node.lines||[];
if(!lines.length){finishLines();return;}
st.lineIndex=clamp...
const text=lines[st.lineIndex];
$('dlgText').textContent='';
$('dlgText').classList.toggle('narration', !node.speaker);
st.typing=true; st.fullText=text; st.shown=0;
$('dlgHint').textContent='click, or press space';
const speed=Math.max(8, 42*settings.textSpeed); // chars per sec
let last=performance.now();
function tick(){
 if(!st.typing||dialogueState!==st) return;
 const now=performance.now(); const add=Math.max(1,Math.floor((now-last)/1000*speed)); last=now;
 st.shown=Math.min(text.length, st.shown+add);
 $('dlgText').textContent=text.slice(0,st.shown);
 if(st.shown>=text.length){ st.typing=false; lineDone(); }
 else st.timer=setTimeout(tick,16);
}
st.timer=setTimeout(tick,20);
```
- Unicode: text.slice okay for accents but not surrogate pairs; fine. Could Array.from but length. Use array. `const chars=Array.from(text);` and join. Do that.
- `lineDone`: if lineIndex < lines.length-1: `$('dlgHint').textContent='click to continue'`; else finishLines().
- `completeTyping`: set typing false, clear timer, text full, lineDone.
- `advanceDialogue`: if typing -> complete; else if awaitingClose -> close; else if lineIndex < lines.length-1 -> lineIndex++ showLine; else finishLines? But lineDone already called finishLines. If topics shown, advancing shouldn't do anything. We need state `topicsShown` or `awaitingTopic`. Add st.phase = 'line'|'topics'|'close'. 
  - After finishLines with topics -> st.phase='topics'. Advance does nothing (or maybe choose?).
  - If no topics and not end -> st.phase='close'; advance closes.
  - If end -> close immediately in finishLines? Better wait for click after last line? Typically auto-close on last click. Since lineDone called after typing complete, user might not have read? The text is visible. Could set phase='close' and hint "click to close" rather than auto-close. But for end nodes (Theo letter) we want after last line click to close and open inspect. Good. For node with end, set phase='close' and on advance close+onEnd. For mara end path, same. For no topics, allowLeave true, same.
  - For node.back -> return to parent immediately after line? Data back nodes are short replies; auto return after last line could be okay, but user may want to read. Better set phase='close' with hint "click to continue" and on advance return parent. So finishLines:
```
if(node.end){ st.phase='close'; st.closeAction='end'; hint 'click to finish'; }
else if(node.back){ st.phase='close'; st.closeAction='back'; hint 'click to continue'; }
else if(topics.length){ st.phase='topics'; showTopics(); }
else { st.phase='close'; st.closeAction='close'; hint 'click to close'; }
```
  - `advanceDialogue`:
    - typing -> complete.
    - phase topics -> nothing.
    - phase close -> if closeAction end -> finishEnd(); back -> returnParent(); close -> closeDialogue.
    - phase line -> next line.
- `finishEnd`:
```
const node=st.node; closeDialogue(); if(node.onEnd) setTimeout(()=>node.onEnd(),30);
```
- closeDialogue clears st; but capture node first.
- `returnParent`:
```
const parent=st.stack.pop(); if(!parent){closeDialogue();return;} renderNode(parent,{skipLines:true});
```
- `showTopics`:
```
const st=dialogueState; const node=st.node;
$('dlgTopics').innerHTML='';
const topics=(node.topics||[]).filter(t=>!t.cond||t.cond(S)).filter(t=>!t.once || !S.usedTopics[`${node.speaker}:${t.id}`]);
if(!topics.length){ st.phase='close'; st.closeAction='close'; $('dlgHint').textContent='click to close'; return; }
st.phase='topics'; $('dlgHint').textContent='choose a question';
topics.forEach(t=>{ button...; });
```
- Note cond may reference S. Good.
- `chooseTopic(topic)`:
```
const st=dialogueState; if(!st||st.phase!=='topics') return;
if(topic.once) S.usedTopics[`${st.node.speaker||'x'}:${topic.id}`]=true;
if(topic.note) effect.note(topic.note);
const parent=st.node;
const next = topic.run? topic.run(S): null;
if(next){ st.stack.push(parent); renderNode(next); }
else {
 if(topic.id==='photo_show'){ showTopics(); }
 else closeDialogue();
}
```
- For `photo_show`, openInspect is called inside run; then we re-show topics. Good. But `showTopics()` uses current node; yes.
- For topic run that returns node with back true, stack parent. Good.
- For nested topics returned node with its own topics and no back, stack still has parent; if user selects topic within that node and run returns node, stack pushes node too. Fine.
- For node end path, onEnd.
- `closeDialogue` clears timer; hides overlay; AUDIO.setDialogue(false); dialogueState=null; `lastPortrait=null`? Keep portrait maybe. Set null.
- `closeOverlay('dialogue')` should also handle. We'll call closeDialogue from closeOverlay? Avoid recursion: closeOverlay can clear st. Implement `closeDialogue()` directly hide and remove from stack via `hideOverlay` internal. Let's define:
```
function hideOverlayEl(id){...}
function closeOverlay(id){
 if(id==='dialogue'){ closeDialogue(); return; }
 ...
}
```
- closeDialogue:
```
const st=dialogueState; if(st&&st.timer)clearTimeout(st.timer);
dialogueState=null;
const el=$('dialogue'); el.classList.add('hidden');
overlayStack=overlayStack.filter(x=>x!=='dialogue');
AUDIO.setDialogue(false);
updatePrompt();
```
- `showOverlay('dialogue',{exclusive:true})` closes others; okay.
- closeAllOverlays loops and calls closeOverlay, which handles dialogue.

- Typewriter timer set; if close, clear.

- `dlgClose.hidden` false/true.

- `startDialogue(node)`:
```
if(!node) return;
ensureAudio();
closeAllOverlays(true)? We want if no other. Use showOverlay('dialogue',{exclusive:true});
dialogueState={node:null,stack:[],...};
AUDIO.setDialogue(true);
renderNode(node);
```
- If already dialogue open and starting new, close first? Set st new. Fine.
- `showOverlay` exclusive will close inspect etc. If called from world.
- If startDialogue called while inspect open? not.

- On topic `photo_show`, openInspect uses showOverlay('inspect') default stacked. Good.

- On Theo end onEnd calls closeDialogue and setTimeout openInspect. Our finishEnd calls closeDialogue then onEnd after 30ms. onEnd calls closeDialogue again safe, then openInspect. Good.
- On finishIntro onEnd calls closeDialogue? finishIntro itself closes. It will be called after close; safe.

- For node `end:true` but also onEnd and `allowLeave` maybe. Good.

- For maraIntroWatch2 'yes' end path: finishEnd close -> onEnd finishIntro -> openInspect. Good.

- `closeDialogue` from X should not call onEnd. Good.

- `renderNode` onEnter for returned nodes? Data rarely. Fine.

- `node.note` from topic node? The note is on the returned node in data (e.g. wren town has note 'wren_town' on extra). `renderNode` handles.

- `speaker` for narration null. Good.

- `D.dialogues.maraIntro` node allowLeave false. Hide X. Good.

- `dlgText` class narration.

- `dlgHint` text.

- `dlgPortrait` hidden via display style; CSS `.dialogue.narration .dlg-portrait` also. Good.

- `dlgName` in narration hidden via CSS head display none. Good.

- `dlgRole`.

- Need set `dlgClose.hidden` for allowLeave false; hidden attr. Good.

